271 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (There is a new segment of journalism and press emerging in the online forum, specially via social platforms like You Tube, Instagram, X \(Twitter\), etc with You Tube having currently 460 million users in the most populous democracies of the world. In 2023, the BJP government banned a documentary by BBC on the Gujarat riots. Still, these platforms have played an important role in the general elections with their growing viewership specially amongst the younger generation. But due to the IT rules 2023 and the Digital personal data protection act 2021, their freedom is being curbed, with the government citing reasons such as national security and spreading of misinformation. While one should note that many such creators on various platforms have been arrested on charges for spreading hate speech and misinformation. In 2023, government banned 8 You Tube channels for spreading fake information by declaration of early Lok Sabha results. During the pandemic, many platforms were accuses of spreading fear about the vaccines and during the recent India-Pakistan tensions, the Indian media was accused of spreading false information about the situation creating tensions at the international level. Hence, it is worthy to think how much regulation is really needed for press and specially the many growing digital platforms with millions of viewers. While freedom of speech and expression is important for a democracy like India, so is maintenance of its internal security and unity among the populace. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [12 13]
>>
