/E (prominent personalities have been its victims. With lack of regulations, it is very difficult to identify real and fake videos and is a very easy means to spread false information and creating panic among people. In May 2024, a man in UP was arrested was generating deepfake of CM Yogi Adityanath referring to the Pulwama attack. The highest fake news via AI generated videos and voice clones surged in May 2024 showing fake exit polls and fake audio clips falsely claiming the resignation of Rahul Gandhi. On May 6, 2024, just before the third phase of the General Election, the Election Commission of India \(ECI\) issued a directive to all political parties to remove AI-generated disinformation within three hours. As per Millenium Post, political parties invested an estimated $50 million during elections to garners support and engagement from the public. Deepfake Analysis Unit set under the Misinformation Combat Alliance is a unique initiative to allow users to send fake news and misinformation generated by Artificial Intelligence via WhatsApp. Artificial intelligence is a new platform with a lot of untapped potential which if regulated can be a new revolution towards freedom of speech and information in the most populated democracies of India. )
