/E (After India attained independence in 1947, the offence of sedition continued to remain in operation under 124A of the IPC. Even though sedition was expressly excluded by the Constituent Assembly as a ground for the limitation of the right to freedom of speech and expression, this right was still being curbed under the guise of this provision of the IPC. On three significant occasions, the constitutionality of this provision was challenged in the courts. These cases shaped the subsequent discourse in the law of sedition.)
